      ],
      "title": "Oscillations directly influence spiking via ephaptic coupling",
      "gist": "Electric fields from oscillations nudge nearby neurons' voltages without synapses, and because they spread widely and nearly instantly, they can coordinate large neuron groups faster than spikes and synapses can.",
      "sourceHeading": "Oscillations directly influence spiking via ephaptic coupling"
    },
